{{!
    @template mod_naas/admin_action_button

    Action button on the Nugget plugin administration page (Test connection,
    Refresh cache). The mod_naas/action_button AMD module reads the data
    attributes, calls the web service and fills the result region.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * buttonid - HTML id of the button
    * resultid - HTML id of the result region
    * methodname - Web service the button calls
    * label - Visible button label
    * pendinglabel - Label shown while the request is in flight
    * successstring - mod_naas string key shown on success
    * failurestring - mod_naas string key shown on failure without a message

    Example context (json):
    {
        "buttonid": "testconnection",
        "resultid": "connection-result",
        "methodname": "mod_naas_test_config",
        "label": "Test connection",
        "pendinglabel": "Testing…",
        "successstring": "connection_test_success",
        "failurestring": "connection_test_failed"
    }
}}
<button type="button"
        class="btn btn-secondary"
        id="{{buttonid}}"
        data-methodname="{{methodname}}"
        data-result-id="{{resultid}}"
        data-success-string="{{successstring}}"
        data-failure-string="{{failurestring}}"
        data-testing-label="{{pendinglabel}}">
    {{label}}
</button>
<div id="{{resultid}}"
     class="connection-result mt-2"
     role="status"
     aria-live="polite"
     hidden></div>
